=== HINT 1 ===
typeof(a) gives you the type of 'a' at compile time.
Use it to declare a temporary variable: typeof(a) _tmp = (a);

=== HINT 2 ===
The three-step swap pattern:
  typeof(a) _tmp = (a);
  (a) = (b);
  (b) = _tmp;

=== HINT 3 ===
Wrap in a block statement ({ ... }) so the tmp variable is scoped:
  #define SWAP(a, b) do { typeof(a) _t = (a); (a) = (b); (b) = _t; } while(0)
The do { } while(0) idiom makes the macro safe in if/else without braces.

=== HINT 4 (SPOILER) ===
#define SWAP(a, b) do { typeof(a) _t = (a); (a) = (b); (b) = _t; } while(0)
